Build the repository row model: grouping, search, sort
All pure, all unit-tested, no React. New files under `applications/openthrottle-developer/app/routing/settings/repositories/`:

**`config/repositories.defaults.ts`** — `REPOSITORIES_DEFAULT_LIMIT`, plus `REPOSITORIES_SORT_BY` / `REPOSITORIES_SORT_ORDER` as `as const` arrays with derived types (mirror `~/routing/projects/config`, and `ProjectsToolbar`'s use of `PROJECTS_SORT_BY`). No enums.

**`data/types.ts`** — the row type. One row = one checkout, carrying its parent repository context:
```
interface RepositoryCheckoutRow {
  branch: string | null;
  checkout: RepositoryCheckoutFieldsFragment;
  children?: RepositoryCheckoutRow[];
  isWorktree: boolean;
  repositoryId: string;
  repositoryName: string;
  remoteUrl: string | null;
}
```

**`utils/rows.ts`** — `buildRepositoryRows(repositories)`: for each repository, the `kind === 'primary'` checkout becomes the parent and `kind === 'worktree'` checkouts become `children`. Handle the real-world edge cases explicitly and test each: a repository with zero checkouts (skip, or emit a parent-less placeholder — decide and document), a repository with several `primary` checkouts (each becomes its own parent row), and worktrees with no primary sibling (promote the first to parent rather than dropping it). Branch resolves as `checkout.inspection?.git.currentBranch ?? repository.defaultBranch ?? null`.

**`utils/search.ts`** — `filterRepositoryRows(rows, search)`: case-insensitive match over repository name, `displayName`, `filesystemPath`, `normalizedRemoteUrl`, and branch. A child match retains the parent; a parent match retains all children. Also return the set of parent row ids that matched only via a child, so the table can auto-expand them.

**`utils/sorting.ts`** — `sortRepositoryRows(rows, sortBy, sortOrder)` over name / updatedAt / checkout count. Children sort within their parent only.

**Done when:** `__tests__` cover every branch above (including the three grouping edge cases and child-match-pulls-parent), and `:lint` / `:typecheck` / `:test` are green for `openthrottle-developer`.
Pure utils + types that turn WorkspaceRepositoryFieldsFragment[] into nested parent/child rows, with search and sort, under app/routing/settings/repositories/.
Plan: Repositories route: nested table + toolbar + pagination

Add searchGitBranches to SkillUsageEventsService (SQL search + ordering + cap)
In `packages/nestjs-repositories/src/modules/skill-usage-events/skill-usage-events.service.ts` add a `searchGitBranches` method plus its result types.

Shape:

```ts
export interface SkillUsageGitBranchRow {
  readonly branch: string;
  readonly count: number;
}

export interface SkillUsageGitBranchSearchResult {
  readonly hasMore: boolean;
  readonly items: readonly SkillUsageGitBranchRow[];
}

searchGitBranches(query: {
  readonly end: string;
  readonly limit?: number | null;
  readonly query?: string | null;
  readonly skillName?: string | null;
  readonly start: string;
}): Promise<SkillUsageGitBranchSearchResult>
```

Implementation notes:
- Build on the existing `dateRangeQuery` helper (half-open `[start, endExclusive)`) and the same `skillName` narrowing `listFilterOptions` uses.
- `git_branch IS NOT NULL AND git_branch <> ''`, `GROUP BY e.git_branch`, `addSelect('COUNT(*)', 'count')`.
- Search: trim the incoming query; when non-empty add `e.git_branch ILIKE :pattern` with a parameterized `%…%`. Escape `%`, `_`, and `\` in the user input first (small exported `escapeLikePattern` util with its own test) so a branch named `feat/100%_done` can't wildcard.
- Ordering in SQL: `.orderBy('(e.git_branch <> :defaultBranch)', 'ASC').addOrderBy('e.git_branch', 'ASC')` with `defaultBranch = 'main'`. Postgres sorts `false` before `true`, so `main` lands first and everything else is A–Z. Define `SKILL_USAGE_DEFAULT_BRANCHES = ['main', 'master'] as const` and pin whichever is present (main wins when both are).
- `limit`: default 20, clamp to `[1, 50]`. Fetch `limit + 1` rows to compute `hasMore`, then slice back to `limit`.

Also cap `listFilterOptions` (both branches and cwds) at 50 so the legacy field can't return an unbounded array.

Tests in `skill-usage-events.service.test.ts`: default ordering puts `main` first then alphabetical; a `master`-only dataset pins `master`; ILIKE is case-insensitive and substring-matching; LIKE metacharacters are escaped, not honored; `limit` clamps and `hasMore` flips correctly; `skillName` narrows; empty range returns `{ hasMore: false, items: [] }`.
Plan: /usage branch filter: searchable dropdown + lazy branch-search API

Rewrite the loader to await plan+tasks and return naked promises for the rest
Rewrite `loader` in `applications/openthrottle-developer/app/routes/plans.$planId._index.tsx`, following the precedent in `app/routes/dashboard._index.tsx:52-84` (fire everything concurrently, return unawaited promises, let RR8 Single Fetch stream them).

Shape:

```ts
export const loader = async (args: Route.LoaderArgs) => {
  const { planId } = args.params;
  if (!planId) return { /* empty shape, promises resolved to empty */ };

  // Kick every request off before the first await so nothing waterfalls.
  const criticalPromise = executeGraphqlWithAuth(args.request, PlanDetailCriticalDocument, { planId });
  const enabledEditors = loadEnabledEditors(args.request);
  const ledger = executeGraphqlWithAuth(args.request, PlanDetailLedgerDocument, { planId }).then(…);
  const outputChunks = …;
  const runHistory = …;
  const tagVocabulary = …;
  const workspaceRepositories = …;

  const critical = await criticalPromise;

  return { enabledEditors, ledger, outputChunks, plan: critical.plan ?? null, runHistory, tagVocabulary, tasks: critical.tasksByPlanId ?? [], workspaceRepositories };
};
```

Rules:
- Every deferred promise must `.then()` into exactly the shape the consumer wants (arrays, defaulted to `[]`) so components never reach into query envelopes. Mirror the dashboard loader's `.then()` mapping.
- Do NOT `.catch()` the deferred promises. Rejections are the point — each region's `errorElement` handles its own failure, and a `workspaceRepositories` failure must no longer 500 the page. `loadEnabledEditors` keeps its internal catch (it already degrades to `[]`).
- The `!planId` short circuit must keep returning the same key set, with the deferred keys as already-resolved promises (`Promise.resolve([])`) so the component's boundaries stay type-uniform.
- Comment the split at the top of the loader: which key is awaited and why, and the standing rule that new fields default to deferred.

Update `app/routes/__tests__/plans.$planId._index.loader.test.ts`: it currently routes mock responses by document identity — extend `mockDocuments` to route all six documents, assert that `plan`/`tasks` come back resolved, that the deferred keys are promises, that each resolves to the mapped shape, and add a case proving a rejected `workspaceRepositories` promise does not make the loader throw.
The core change: time-to-render becomes the cost of PlanDetailCritical instead of the slowest field in the page.
Plan: Fast plan-detail route: stream the heavy tabs, paint the shell first

Replace the scheme-only deep-link config with a capability-aware plan-launch builder
`WORKSPACE_EDITOR_DEEP_LINKS` currently carries just `{ label, scheme }`, which cannot express the three editors' genuinely different URL shapes (see the plan description's capability table). Rework it into a per-editor descriptor plus a builder, with unit tests.

Shape to aim for (adjust naming to fit the repo):

```ts
interface PlanLaunchTarget {
  readonly buildHref: (input: { readonly planId: string; readonly workingDirectory: string }) => string | null;
  readonly label: string;
  readonly supportsFolder: boolean;
  readonly supportsPrompt: boolean;
}
```

Per-editor builders — use `URLSearchParams` for every query value (all params must be URL-encoded):
- **Claude**: `claude://code/new?` + `URLSearchParams({ folder, q: `/ot-claude-loop ${planId}` })`. The slash command must be first on line 1 of `q`.
- **Cursor**: `cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/prompt?` + `URLSearchParams({ text })` where text names the skill file (`Run OpenThrottle plan <planId> following .agents/skills/ot-claude-loop/SKILL.md`). Cursor's deeplink takes **no folder param** — the prompt lands in whatever Cursor window is focused. Decide here whether Cursor ships with a tooltip stating that, or is omitted from the toolbar; record the decision in the file's JSDoc either way.
- **VS Code**: keep reusing `editorHref({ absolutePath, scheme: 'vscode' })` from `@openthrottle/react-router-ide` — open-folder only. Do not invent a prompt param; `microsoft/vscode#279701` is still open.

Return `null` from `buildHref` when the target's required input is missing (e.g. no working directory for a folder-based editor) so callers can skip the button instead of rendering a dead link.

Add co-located tests asserting: exact Claude href for a known planId + path, encoding of a path containing spaces and `#`, Cursor href has no folder, VS Code href is unchanged from today's `editorHref` output, and `null` on missing input.

Validate: `pnpm nx run openthrottle-developer:typecheck` and the new test file.
Plan: PlanEditorActions: one-click "open this plan in my editor" deep links

Build GlobalPopover in react-router-ui-global
Add `GlobalPopover` to `packages/react-router-ui-global`.

**Read the reference first**: `applications/openthrottle-developer/app/routing/settings/repositories/components/RepositoryRowActions.tsx` (the `/settings/repositories` route). That file is the model — the API below is a generalization of what it already does, and the thinner queues menu (`routing/queues/data/queues-table-columns.tsx`) must fit inside the same API.

Scaffold — do not hand-write the file:

```bash
NX_ISOLATE_PLUGINS=false pnpm nx g @tools/generators:react-router --subGenerator=component --describe
```

use the sub-generator that targets a package (confirm exact flags with `--describe`; `--folder` takes the full path, e.g. `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/components`).

**Implementation**

- Build on the shadcn `DropdownMenu` family re-exported from `@openthrottle/react-router-shadcn` (`DropdownMenu`, `DropdownMenuTrigger`, `DropdownMenuContent`, `DropdownMenuLabel`, `DropdownMenuSeparator`, `DropdownMenuItem`) plus `AlertDialog*` for the confirm path — see the plan description for why this is a DropdownMenu despite the name.
- Default trigger: a `ghost` `size="icon"` `Button` (`className="size-7"`) with `MoreHorizontalIcon` (`size-4`, `aria-hidden`) and a required `aria-label`, matching `RepositoryRowActions` today. Allow a `trigger` override slot.
- `align` defaults to `'end'`; the wrapper is `flex justify-end`.

**Props (target shape — adjust names only if lint/type reality forces it)**

```ts
export type GlobalPopoverAction =
  | { confirm?: GlobalPopoverConfirm; destructive?: boolean; disabled?: boolean; fields: Record<string, string>; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'submit'; label: string; method?: 'post'; pending?: boolean; pendingLabel?: string; separatorBefore?: boolean }
  | { disabled?: boolean; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'link'; label: string; separatorBefore?: boolean; to: string }
  | { disabled?: boolean; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'select'; label: string; onSelect: () => void; separatorBefore?: boolean };

export interface GlobalPopoverConfirm {
  cancelLabel?: string;
  confirmLabel?: string;
  description: React.ReactNode;
  title: string;
}

export interface GlobalPopoverProps {
  actions: GlobalPopoverAction[];
  align?: 'center' | 'end' | 'start';
  ariaLabel: string;
  className?: string;
  heading?: string;
  testId?: string;
  trigger?: React.ReactNode;
}
```

- `kind: 'submit'` renders a `Form method="post"` with hidden inputs from `fields` and a submit `button` inside `DropdownMenuItem asChild` — exactly the pattern in `RepositoryRowActions`. `pending: true` disables the item and shows `pendingLabel`; callers derive it from `useNavigation` (keep the derivation at the call site, it's row-specific).
- `confirm` routes the item through `AlertDialog` — the item's `onSelect` calls `event.preventDefault()` and opens the dialog; the actual `Form` submit lives in `AlertDialogAction`. `description` is a `React.ReactNode` so callers can emphasize a name inline.
- `kind: 'link'` renders `DropdownMenuItem asChild` around a `react-router` `Link` with `viewTransition`.
- `kind: 'select'` calls `onSelect`.
- `destructive: true` applies `text-destructive`; `separatorBefore` emits a `DropdownMenuSeparator`.

**Boundaries**

- Discriminated union per `.agents/rules/coding/discriminated-unions.mdc`; no enums, no `as` casts, explicit return types, `import type` for types.
- Component file exports only `GlobalPopover`, `GlobalPopoverProps`, and the closely-related action/confirm types. Default copy (fallback confirm labels, `Actions` header text) goes in `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/data/data.copy.ts`.
- Keep the six section markers and the 210-line cap — the confirm wrapper will likely need to be its own sibling component file (one component per file).
- Export from `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/index.ts`, alphabetized with the other `./components/Global*` exports. Tag package public API exports with JSDoc `@public` so Knip keeps them.

**Also add** the canonical actions-column header so tables stop hand-rolling it: a `GLOBAL_POPOVER_COPY.actionsHeader` constant (`'Actions'`) and a right-aligned header renderer matching the current queues markup — `<div className="py-2 text-right"><span className="text-sm font-medium">Actions</span></div>` — in its own file if it needs to be a component.

**Tests** — `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/components/__tests__/GlobalPopover.test.tsx`, using `component` (not `screen`) and `userEvent` (not `fireEvent`), inside a `createRoutesStub`/memory router so `Link` and `Form` resolve. Cover: trigger opens the menu; each of the three action kinds renders and fires; `pending` shows `pendingLabel` and blocks activation; `disabled` blocks activation; `separatorBefore` renders a separator; a `confirm` action opens the dialog and only submits after confirming (and not on cancel).

**Validate**

```bash
pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:lint && pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:typecheck && pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:test
```

plus `pnpm run audit:component-shape`. Run targets sequentially, never `--parallel`.
Added GlobalPopover (+ ActionItem, ConfirmDialog, ActionsHeader) to @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global with submit/link/select actions, confirm path, GLOBAL_POPOVER_COPY, package exports, and tests. Validated lint/typecheck/test/audit:component-shape. Commit 82153bc6.
Plan: Normalize table row Actions on a shared GlobalPopover
